2025-04-06 15:06:14 INFO  s.u.e.m.MonopolizingConvoApplication - 	 32 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=316, text='Different operating systems have different conventions for line endings. This is not related to Python just how the systems themselves work.', sender='Katriel', sentTime=Wed Jan 08 07:27:30 CST 2020}
2025-04-06 15:06:14 INFO  s.u.e.m.MonopolizingConvoApplication - 	 33 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=316, text='yes...?', sender='Aisley', sentTime=Wed Jan 08 07:27:40 CST 2020}
2025-04-06 15:06:14 INFO  s.u.e.m.MonopolizingConvoApplication - 	 34 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=316, text='On Linux a newline is simply a `\` character a newline character', sender='Katriel', sentTime=Wed Jan 08 07:27:42 CST 2020}
2025-04-06 15:06:14 INFO  s.u.e.m.MonopolizingConvoApplication - 	 35 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=316, text='yes', sender='Aisley', sentTime=Wed Jan 08 07:27:46 CST 2020}
2025-04-06 15:06:14 INFO  s.u.e.m.MonopolizingConvoApplication - 	 36 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=316, text='But on Windows it's actually a combination of two characters in a file: `\\r\`', sender='Katriel', sentTime=Wed Jan 08 07:28:00 CST 2020}
2025-04-06 15:06:14 INFO  s.u.e.m.MonopolizingConvoApplication - 	 37 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=316, text='hmm', sender='Aisley', sentTime=Wed Jan 08 07:28:06 CST 2020}
2025-04-06 15:06:14 INFO  s.u.e.m.MonopolizingConvoApplication - 	 38 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=316, text='And I think it was on Apple but some system at least used to sue `\\\r`', sender='Katriel', sentTime=Wed Jan 08 07:28:20 CST 2020}
2025-04-06 15:06:14 INFO  s.u.e.m.MonopolizingConvoApplication - 	 39 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=316, text='It\'s a legacy from typewriters where you had to go to the next line AND return the carriage of letters back to the start of the line', sender='Katriel', sentTime=Wed Jan 08 07:28:51 CST 2020}
2025-04-06 15:06:14 INFO  s.u.e.m.MonopolizingConvoApplication - 	 40 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=316, text='Hence: return carriage to start; newline', sender='Katriel', sentTime=Wed Jan 08 07:29:03 CST 2020}
2025-04-06 15:06:14 INFO  s.u.e.m.MonopolizingConvoApplication - 	 41 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=316, text='right?', sender='Aisley', sentTime=Wed Jan 08 07:29:10 CST 2020}
2025-04-06 15:06:14 INFO  s.u.e.m.MonopolizingConvoApplication - 	 42 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=316, text='So they used \ to go to new line and \\r to go to the first of the new line?', sender='Aisley', sentTime=Wed Jan 08 07:29:20 CST 2020}
2025-04-06 15:06:14 INFO  s.u.e.m.MonopolizingConvoApplication - 	 43 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=316, text='Yes', sender='Katriel', sentTime=Wed Jan 08 07:29:26 CST 2020}
2025-04-06 15:06:14 INFO  s.u.e.m.MonopolizingConvoApplication - 	 44 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=316, text='It's a leftover from digital typewriters where the text was temporarily stored first and then used to control/print the text using the typewriter hardware', sender='Katriel', sentTime=Wed Jan 08 07:29:56 CST 2020}
2025-04-06 15:06:14 INFO  s.u.e.m.MonopolizingConvoApplication - 	 45 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=316, text='Anyway Linux simplified it to a single character since it's no longer needed', sender='Katriel', sentTime=Wed Jan 08 07:30:11 CST 2020}
2025-04-06 15:06:14 INFO  s.u.e.m.MonopolizingConvoApplication - 	 46 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=316, text='Windows having much older roots still uses `\\r\`', sender='Katriel', sentTime=Wed Jan 08 07:30:21 CST 2020}
2025-04-06 15:06:14 INFO  s.u.e.m.MonopolizingConvoApplication - 	 47 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=316, text='> It's a leftover from digital typewriters where the text was temporarily stored first and then used to control/print the text using the typewriter hardware', sender='Aisley', sentTime=Wed Jan 08 07:30:33 CST 2020}
2025-04-06 15:06:14 INFO  s.u.e.m.MonopolizingConvoApplication - 	 48 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=316, text='Didn't understand this part', sender='Aisley', sentTime=Wed Jan 08 07:30:36 CST 2020}
2025-04-06 15:06:14 INFO  s.u.e.m.MonopolizingConvoApplication - 	 49 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=316, text='They first made the text and then printed it? Instead of doing it at the same time by printing?', sender='Aisley', sentTime=Wed Jan 08 07:30:55 CST 2020}
2025-04-06 15:06:14 INFO  s.u.e.m.MonopolizingConvoApplication - 	 50 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=316, text='There was a time where we had digital type writers: You typed in a line and you could edit it before it was actually typed. That way you could correct typing mistakes without the tippex before they were actually on paper.', sender='Katriel', sentTime=Wed Jan 08 07:32:13 CST 2020}
