2025-04-06 15:06:14 INFO  s.u.e.m.MonopolizingConvoApplication - 	 21 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=465, text='Catastrophic backtracking is a real problem and it's one this server isn't new to', sender='Antonie', sentTime=Fri Apr 10 09:38:28 CDT 2020}
2025-04-06 15:06:14 INFO  s.u.e.m.MonopolizingConvoApplication - 	 22 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=465, text='even @Python suffered from that issue', sender='Antonie', sentTime=Fri Apr 10 09:38:33 CDT 2020}
2025-04-06 15:06:14 INFO  s.u.e.m.MonopolizingConvoApplication - 	 23 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=465, text='I remember I was trying to write a regex to match every possible url when I first learned about regexes. I imagined the power that I had just learned and how many things I could do as a result of it. But I ended up finding there was no way to accurately match everything perfectly. URLs are too general. If you need something more specific they come in handy. But extremely general regexes just seem to eventually be wrong the more you put different types of data through them. So now any time I use one I just make sure to look at the data I expect to feed it.', sender='Heidy', sentTime=Fri Apr 10 09:40:40 CDT 2020}
2025-04-06 15:06:14 INFO  s.u.e.m.MonopolizingConvoApplication - 	 24 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=465, text='If there was no way that I could look over that data and kind of eyeball what was going on because there was so much of itr I would be averse to using them.', sender='Heidy', sentTime=Fri Apr 10 09:40:59 CDT 2020}
2025-04-06 15:06:14 INFO  s.u.e.m.MonopolizingConvoApplication - 	 25 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=465, text='I've written a regex like that', sender='Antonie', sentTime=Fri Apr 10 09:41:00 CDT 2020}
