2025-04-06 17:14:27 INFO  s.u.e.m.file.util.TextFileExport - 	 1 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=588, text='if you want to do this dynamically without knowing what the parent/grandparent class is you can use the `__mro__` property of classes (short for method resolution order"). so:```pythonclass GrandChild(Parent): def __init__(self): grandparent_class = type(self).__mro__[2] grandparent_class.__init__(self)```this is assuming there\'s no multiple inheritance (all these classes only inherit from one class).', sender='Mianna', sentTime=Tue Dec 17 06:43:46 CST 2019}
2025-04-06 17:14:27 INFO  s.u.e.m.file.util.TextFileExport - 	 2 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=588, text='with multiple inheritance you can use the length of the `__bases__` attribute to figure out how many spaces to skip in the `__mro__` to get the first grandparent class.', sender='Mianna', sentTime=Tue Dec 17 06:47:07 CST 2019}
2025-04-06 17:14:27 INFO  s.u.e.m.file.util.TextFileExport - 	 3 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=587, text='so```pygrandparent_class = type(self).__mro__[ len(type(self).__bases__)+1]```', sender='Mianna', sentTime=Tue Dec 17 06:48:57 CST 2019}
2025-04-06 17:14:27 INFO  s.u.e.m.file.util.TextFileExport - 	 4 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=588, text='but still there may be multiple grandparent classes.so the better option would be to get the bases of each class in `__bases__`', sender='Mianna', sentTime=Tue Dec 17 06:51:03 CST 2019}
2025-04-06 17:14:27 INFO  s.u.e.m.file.util.TextFileExport - 	 5 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=587, text='```pydef grandparents(cls): seen = set() for parent in cls.__bases__: for grandparent in parent.__bases__: if grandparent not in seen: yield grandparent seen.add(grandparent)```', sender='Mianna', sentTime=Tue Dec 17 06:52:14 CST 2019}
2025-04-06 17:14:27 INFO  s.u.e.m.file.util.TextFileExport - 	 6 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=588, text='something like that', sender='Mianna', sentTime=Tue Dec 17 06:52:28 CST 2019}
2025-04-06 17:14:27 INFO  s.u.e.m.file.util.TextFileExport - 	 7 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=588, text='oh also just remembered about `__base__ ` and `__class__`', sender='Mianna', sentTime=Tue Dec 17 07:15:05 CST 2019}
2025-04-06 17:14:27 INFO  s.u.e.m.file.util.TextFileExport - 	 8 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=588, text='so```pythongrandparent_class = __class__.__base__.__base__```could work too (if no multiple inheritance)', sender='Mianna', sentTime=Tue Dec 17 07:15:38 CST 2019}
