2025-04-06 17:14:27 INFO  s.u.e.m.file.util.TextFileExport - 	 1 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=263, text='@gm would you typically store different constant types in classes? for example  if ( in the `constants.py` file ) there are a few different types such as `directories` `files` and `variables` would it makes sense to store these within three classes or just have them flat? Having them in classes might make it clearer what they are when called from other files so that's more explicit (good)... but I'm not mutating the data just providing and don't need any methods so perhaps a class is an abuse 🤔', sender='Asif', sentTime=Tue Jan 07 02:21:09 CST 2020}
