2025-04-06 17:14:27 INFO  s.u.e.m.file.util.TextFileExport - 	 25 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=263, text='okay say you have some function that takes in some data and returns 3 metrics:```pythondef f(data_1 data_2): ... return metric_1 metric_2 metric_3```', sender='Sifeddine', sentTime=Tue Jan 07 02:29:06 CST 2020}
2025-04-06 17:14:27 INFO  s.u.e.m.file.util.TextFileExport - 	 26 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=263, text='you could return the result as a bare `tuple`', sender='Sifeddine', sentTime=Tue Jan 07 02:29:11 CST 2020}
2025-04-06 17:14:27 INFO  s.u.e.m.file.util.TextFileExport - 	 27 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=263, text='so assuming you took in `numpy` arrays the type signature would be:```pythondef f(data_1: np.ndarray data_2: np.ndarray) > Tuple[float float float]```', sender='Sifeddine', sentTime=Tue Jan 07 02:29:45 CST 2020}
2025-04-06 17:14:27 INFO  s.u.e.m.file.util.TextFileExport - 	 28 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=263, text='that'd be the default return i guess yea', sender='Asif', sentTime=Tue Jan 07 02:29:52 CST 2020}
2025-04-06 17:14:27 INFO  s.u.e.m.file.util.TextFileExport - 	 29 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=263, text='alternatively you could define a `dataclass` or a `namedtuple`:```pythonclass MetricsNT(NamedTuple): k: float g: float u_0: float```', sender='Sifeddine', sentTime=Tue Jan 07 02:30:26 CST 2020}
2025-04-06 17:14:27 INFO  s.u.e.m.file.util.TextFileExport - 	 30 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=263, text='see the `dataclass` documentation for the equivalent', sender='Sifeddine', sentTime=Tue Jan 07 02:30:35 CST 2020}
2025-04-06 17:14:27 INFO  s.u.e.m.file.util.TextFileExport - 	 31 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=263, text='then you would return `MetricsNT(metric_1 metric_2 metric_3)`', sender='Sifeddine', sentTime=Tue Jan 07 02:30:48 CST 2020}
2025-04-06 17:14:27 INFO  s.u.e.m.file.util.TextFileExport - 	 32 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=263, text='the main difference between a `namedtuple` and a `dataclass` is that `dataclasses` are not `tuples` and therefore do not support destructuring', sender='Sifeddine', sentTime=Tue Jan 07 02:31:07 CST 2020}
2025-04-06 17:14:27 INFO  s.u.e.m.file.util.TextFileExport - 	 33 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=263, text='i.e. you can still do `k g u_0 = f(data_1 data_2)` if it returns a `namedtuple` but not if it returns a `dataclass`', sender='Sifeddine', sentTime=Tue Jan 07 02:31:32 CST 2020}
2025-04-06 17:14:27 INFO  s.u.e.m.file.util.TextFileExport - 	 34 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=263, text='I think the syntax is something like this:```python@dataclass(frozen=True)class MetricsDC: k: float g: float u_0: float```', sender='Sifeddine', sentTime=Tue Jan 07 02:31:59 CST 2020}
