2025-04-06 17:14:27 INFO  s.u.e.m.file.util.TextFileExport - 	 9 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=316, text='if we used \\r before our string like \\r"Hello \ Bye" it would print Hello \ Bye right? But if we used it in our string like "Hello \\r Bye" what was the result exactly? HelloByeor ByeHello?', sender='Aisley', sentTime=Wed Jan 08 07:22:13 CST 2020}
2025-04-06 17:14:27 INFO  s.u.e.m.file.util.TextFileExport - 	 10 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=316, text='Ah you're mixing two things up. The `\\r` is the carriage return character. You don't use it in front of a string that's just an `r` by itself to turn it into a raw string.', sender='Katriel', sentTime=Wed Jan 08 07:23:19 CST 2020}
2025-04-06 17:14:27 INFO  s.u.e.m.file.util.TextFileExport - 	 11 Msg: MessageAnalysisVO{disentangledId=316, text='Ik that it's usage is different if it's before or in the string', sender='Aisley', sentTime=Wed Jan 08 07:24:08 CST 2020}
